:: Mansion Cemetery
<<location "abandoned_mansion">>
<<if $phase is 1>>
	The ever denser woods at once give way, opening onto large, rusted gates. Whatever lock holds them shut has long since fallen apart, allowing you entry. Behind them lies an old cemetery and an even older, decrepit manor. 
	<br><br>
	You push the gate ajar, stepping inside.
	<br><br>
<</if>>
	You are in the forest cemetery. An old manor looms from a hill, surrounded by stone ruins. It's quiet.
	<br><br>
	<<if !$plants_known.includes("honeysuckle")>>
		<<link [[Search for Seeds (0:30)|Honeysuckle Seeds]]>><<set $plants_known.push("honeysuckle")>><<pass 30>><</link>>
		<br>
	<</if>>
	<<link [[Tend to the Gravestones (0:30)|Forest Mansion Graves]]>><<tending 2>><<tiredness 2>><<trauma -2>><<pass 30>><</link>><<gtending>><<gtiredness>><<ltrauma>>
	<br>
	<<link [[Leave Flowers for the Dead (0:15)|Forest Mansion Flowers]]>><<world_corruption "soft" -1>><<pass 15>><</link>>
	<br>
	<<link [[Rob a Grave (2:00)|Forest Mansion Graverob]]>><<set $blackmoney += 30>><<crimeUp 30 "thievery">><<pass 120>><<tiredness 5>><</link>><<ggtiredness>><<gcrime "thievery">>
	<br>
	<<link [[Approach the Old Manor (0:10)|Forest Mansion Explore]]>><<pass 10>><</link>>
	<br>
	<<link [[Leave (0:10)|Forest]]>><<pass 10>><</link>>

:: Honeysuckle Seeds
Along the cemetery walls crawl vines upon vines of honeysuckles, many of which hold ripened berries. You pick some, saving the seeds for future use.
<br><br>
<span class="gold">You can now grow <<foodstufficon "honeysuckle">> honeysuckles.</span>
<br><br>
<<link [[Next|Mansion Cemetery]]>><</link>>

:: Forest Mansion Graves
You spend some time cleaning up the cemetery, scrubbing the graves and trimming the greenery that has started to grow over the stones. Taking care of such a meaningful place makes you feel a little better about everything.
<br><br>
/*
<<if C.npc.Evan.love gte 60>>
	You feel eyes on you. When you spin around, you see Evan watching you from the upper floor of the manor. <<His>> eyes settle upon yours, and <<he>> gives a small nod of approval.
	<br><br>
<<elseif $evanmeet is 1>>
	You feel eyes on you. When you spin around, you see Evan watching you from the upper floor of the manor. Though <<he>>'s quick to leave, you swear <<his>> eyes look a little softer than before.
	<br><br>
<</if>>
 */
<<link [[Next|Mansion Cemetery]]>><</link>>

:: Forest Mansion Flowers
You spend a little bit of time setting flowers by some of the many, many graves. When you look across your work, you get this feeling that just a little more is right in the world.
<br><br>
<<link [[Next|Mansion Cemetery]]>><</link>>

:: Forest Mansion Graverob
You take the time to dig up one of the many, many graves. Though exhausting, your efforts bear fruit when you hit something solid, unearthing an old, dirtied coffin. You only pry it open a crack before a rancid smell spills out from the gap. Still, you press on. Backing out now would be worthless. 
<br><br>
Picking the corpse for what value it holds, you end up with a fistful of expensive jewelry. Though you're eager to sell it, it'd be best to wait until you find a buyer who won't ask questions.
<br><br>
/*
<<if C.npc.Evan.love gte 60>>
	<<npc "Evan">><<person1>>
	A voice rings out from behind you. "To think I thought so highly of you." You whip around. <span class="gold">It's Evan.</span> <<He>> looks utterly livid, <<his>> hands balled into tight fists. You see hurt within <<his>> rage. "Clearly, I was mistaken. You're no better than rabble." Before you get the chance to respond, <<he>> vanishes.
	<br><br>
<<elseif $evanmeet is 1>>
	You feel eyes on you. When you spin around, you see Evan watching you from the upper floor of the manor. <<He>> glares at you, <<his>> eyes filled with disgust.
	<br><br>
<</if>>
*/
<<link [[Next|Mansion Cemetery]]>><</link>>

:: Forest Mansion Explore
<<set $outside to 1>><<location "abandoned_mansion">><<set $forestmansionstage to 0>><<effects>>

<<if $foresthunt gte 1 and $edenforesthunt is 1>>
	<<set $rng to random(1, 60)>>
	<<if $rng lte 20>>
	<span class="red">You are being hunted. You see shotgun shells lying on the ground.</span>
	<br><br>
	<<elseif $rng lte 40>>
	<span class="red">You are being hunted. You see boot prints on the ground.</span>
	<br><br>
	<<else>>
	<span class="red"> You are being hunted. You hear a gun firing from afar.</span>
	<br><br>
	<</if>>
<<elseif $foresthunt gte 1 and $blackwolfhunt is 1>>
	<<set $rng to random(1, 60)>>
	<<if $rng lte 20>>
	<span class="red">You are being hunted. You see wolf fur tangled in the trees.</span>
	<br><br>
	<<elseif $rng lte 40>>
	<span class="red">You are being hunted. You see wolf prints on the ground.</span>
	<br><br>
	<<else>>
	<span class="red">You are being hunted. You hear a growl in the distance.</span>
	<br><br>
	<</if>>
<</if>>

<<if $arousal gte 10000>>
	<<orgasmforest>>
<</if>>

<<if $stress gte 10000 and $TaylorWith is 0>>
	<<passoutforest>>
<<elseif $foresthunt gte 10 and $TaylorWith is 0>>
	<<foresthunt>>
<<else>>
	<<set $danger to random(1, 10000)>><<set $dangerevent to 0>>
	<<if $TaylorWith is 1>>
		<<npc Taylor>><<person1>>
		You and Taylor walk through the woods to an old, decrepit mansion. Though covered in foliage and faded by age, a small plaque by the rusted gates tells you where you are. It reads, "Shade Street, Edwin Estate." 
	<<else>>
		You approach the manor atop the hill. The mansion seems a lot bigger up close, towering into the sky. Though covered in foliage and faded by age, a small plaque by the rusted gates tells you where you are. It reads, "Shade Street, Edwin Estate." 
	<</if>>
	<<if $forestmansionpicked is 0>>
		When you arrive at the front steps, you find two large doors blocking your path. They are locked shut. 
		<br><br>
		<<link [[Pick lock (0:05)|Forest Mansion Pick Lock]]>><<pass 5>><</link>>
		<br>
		<<if $ghost gte 1 and $TaylorWith is 0>>
			You can phase through the doors if you concentrate. 
			<br>
			<<link [[Phase (0:01)|Forest Mansion Entrance]]>><<tiredness 20>><<pass 1>><</link>><<ggtiredness>>
			<br>
		<</if>>
	<<else>>
		The front door of the mansion itself is unlocked and slightly ajar. There's no sign of life inside.
		<br><br>

		<<link [[Enter (0:05)|Forest Mansion Entrance]]>><<pass 5>><</link>>
		<br>
	<</if>>
	<<if $TaylorWith is 1>>
		<<link [[Ask Taylor (0:20)|Forest Mansion Look Around]]>><<pass 20>><</link>>
	<<else>>
		<<link [[Look around (0:30)|Forest Mansion Look Around]]>><</link>>
	<</if>>
	<br>
	<<if $TaylorWith is 0 and V.transformationParts.dragon.wings is "default">>
		<<dragonwingsicon>><<link [[Fly somewhere|Fly]]>><</link>>
		<br>
		<<link [[Go back (0:10)|Mansion Cemetery]]>><<pass 10>><</link>>
	<</if>>
<</if>>

:: Forest Mansion Pick Lock
<<set $lock to 1000>>
<<effects>>
<<if $skulduggery gte $lock>>
	<<set $forestmansionpicked to 1>>
	<<skulduggeryskilluse>>
	The lock is like nothing you have ever seen before, but you relish in the challenge. You place your ear against the door while you poke around, trying to fathom its inner workings. Eventually, after one last application of pressure, you hear a heavy click. You successfully unlocked the door.
	<br><br>
	<<if $TaylorWith is 1>>
		<<npcincr Taylor love 3>>
		"Wow that was impressive, I've never seen someone as adept at picking locks. Maybe you should come along more often." <<ggglove>>
		<br><br>
	<</if>>
	<<if $forestmansionstage is 0>>
		<<link [[Enter|Forest Mansion Entrance]]>><</link>>
		<br>
		<<link [[Go back|Forest Mansion Explore]]>><</link>>
	<<else>>
		<<getouticon>><<link [[Leave|Forest Mansion Explore]]>><</link>>
		<br>
		<<link [[Go back|Forest Mansion Entrance]]>><</link>>
	<</if>>
<<else>>
	You start to pick at the lock, but you can't even begin to figure out how it's supposed to work. You refrain from further picking, not wanting to waste time on a futile effort.
	<br><br>
	<<if $forestmansionstage is 0>>
		<<link [[Go back|Forest Mansion Explore]]>><</link>>
	<<else>>
		<<link [[Go back|Forest Mansion Entrance]]>><</link>>
	<</if>>
<</if>>

:: Forest Mansion Look Around
<<effects>>
<<if $forestmansionkitchen is 0>>
	<<set $forestmansionkitchen to 1>>
	<<if $TaylorWith is 1>>
		<<pass 20>>
		Taylor takes a moment to examine the lock and tries to slide a twisted pin into the crack. A cracking sound is heard within the device and the pin returns completely twisted. Taylor grimices.
		<br><br>
		"Yeah sorry, but I can't do anything about this lock. Apparently some people have managed to get their hands on a key but I have no clue where to even begin looking." <<He>> starts to pace. "For now we should just go around and check the windows."
		<br><br>
	<<else>>
		<<pass 30>>
	<</if>>
<<else>>
	<<pass 10>>
<</if>>
<<if $TaylorWith is 1>>
	The two of you circle around the manor, eventually finding an open window. From what you can make out inside, it appears to lead into a kitchen.
<<else>>
	You circle around the manor, eventually finding an open window. From what you can make out inside, it appears to lead into a kitchen.
<</if>>
<br><br>

<<link [[Enter|Forest Mansion Kitchen]]>><</link>>
<br>
<<link [[Go back|Forest Mansion Explore]]>><</link>>

:: Forest Mansion Entrance

<<if $foresthunt gte 1>>
	<span class="lblue">You're relatively safe at this abandoned mansion. Whatever was hunting you will have given up.</span>
	<br><br>
	<<set $foresthunt to 0>>
<</if>>

<<set $outside to 0>><<location "abandoned_mansion">><<set $forestmansionstage to 1>><<effects>>
You find yourself in the mansion's entryway. Dust blankets it in its entirety. A coat rack stands to the side, dressed in an old coat and a hat that is caked with years of grime.
<br><br>
On both your left and right loom hallways loaded with doors. Directly before you stands a staircase that leads upwards.
<br><br>

<<if $rng lte 50 and $eventskip is 0>>
	<<forestmansionrandomevents>>
<<else>>
	<<if $TaylorWith is 1>>
		"This place is still in quite remarkable condition for being as old as it is." Taylor remarks. 
	<</if>>

	There's doors to the left and right as well as a staircase upwards.
	<br><br>

	<<link [[Enter the left hallway (0:05)|Forest Mansion Left Hallway]]>><<pass 5>><<set $eventskip to 0>><<set $rng to random(1,100)>><</link>>
	<br>
	<<link [[Enter the right hallway (0:05)|Forest Mansion Right Hallway]]>><<pass 5>><<set $eventskip to 0>><<set $rng to random(1,100)>><</link>>
	<br>
	<<link [[Go upstairs (0:05)|Forest Mansion Landing]]>><<pass 5>><<set $eventskip to 0>><<set $rng to random(1,100)>><</link>>
	<br>
	<<if $forestmansionpicked is 0>>
		<<if $skulduggery gte $lock>>
			<span class="green">The locks look easy to pick.</span>
			<br><br>
			<<link [[Pick lock (0:05)|Forest Mansion Pick Lock]]>><<pass 5>><</link>>
			<br>
		<<else>>
			<span class="blue">The locks look beyond your ability to pick.</span> <<skulduggeryrequired>>
			<br>
		<</if>>
		<<if $ghost gte 1 and $TaylorWith is 0>>
			You can phase through the doors if you concentrate.
			<br><br>
			<<link [[Phase (0:01)|Forest Mansion Explore]]>><<tiredness 20>><<pass 1>><</link>><<ggtiredness>>
			<br>
		<</if>>
	<<else>>
		<<getouticon>><<link [[Leave (0:05)|Forest Mansion Explore]]>><<pass 5>><</link>>
		<br>
	<</if>>
<</if>>

:: Forest Mansion Left Hallway
<<set $outside to 0>><<location "abandoned_mansion">><<set $forestmansionstage to 2>><<effects>>
You stand in the mansion's left hallway. The floorboards groan beneath each step you take.
<br><br>
Of the many rooms lining the hall, two in particular catch your eye. 
<br><br>

<<if $rng lte 50 and $eventskip is 0>>
	<<forestmansionrandomevents>>
<<else>>
	<<link [[Enter the kitchen (0:05)|Forest Mansion Kitchen]]>><<pass 5>><<set $eventskip to 0>><<set $rng to random(1,100)>><</link>>
	<br>
	<<link [[Enter the dining room (0:05)|Forest Mansion Dining Room]]>><<pass 5>><<set $eventskip to 0>><<set $rng to random(1,100)>><</link>>
	<br>
	<<link [[Towards the entrance (0:05)|Forest Mansion Entrance]]>><<pass 5>><<set $eventskip to 0>><<set $rng to random(1,100)>><</link>>
	<br>
<</if>>

:: Forest Mansion Kitchen

<<if $foresthunt gte 1>>
	<span class="lblue">You're relatively safe at this location. Whatever was hunting you will have given up.</span>
	<br><br>
	<<set $foresthunt to 0>>
<</if>>

<<set $outside to 0>><<location "abandoned_mansion">><<set $forestmansionstage to 3>><<effects>>
You enter a small room chock-full of cooking appliances and utensils from a different age. Both an old wood oven and an ice box rest against the wall, and silverware lines the countertops. In the corner of the room lies a trapdoor that leads deeper. It is covered in dust, having laid untouched for years.
<br><br>
One of the windows is open. 
<br><br>

<<if $rng lte 50 and $eventskip is 0>>
	<<forestmansionrandomevents>>
<<else>>

	<<if $TaylorWith is 1>>
		"This must be the wine cellar. Our town used to pride itself on its high quality wine as a deluxe export. I can't believe some of this stuff still exists."
		<br>
	<</if>>

	<<link [[Go down to the cellar (0:05)|Forest Mansion Cellar]]>><<pass 5>><<set $eventskip to 0>><<set $rng to random(1,100)>><</link>>
	<br>
	<<link [[Go to the hallway (0:05)|Forest Mansion Left Hallway]]>><<pass 5>><<set $eventskip to 0>><<set $rng to random(1,100)>><</link>>
	<br>
	<<if $TaylorWith is 1>>
		<<getouticon>><<link [[Leave through the window|Forest Mansion Taylor Leave]]>><</link>>
		<br>
	<<else>>
		<<getouticon>><<link [[Leave through the window|Forest Mansion Look Around]]>><</link>>
		<br>
	<</if>>
<</if>>

:: Forest Mansion Cellar
<<set $outside to 0>><<location "abandoned_mansion">><<set $forestmansionstage to 4>><<effects>>
Dusting off the trapdoor, you crack it open and peer below. What peers back is an old ladder and an abyss of darkness. Despite the limited vision, you make your way down.
<br><br>
At the bottom is a damp, pitch-black room. Though your eyes adjust to the darkness, you can still only barely make out the details of your environment. There's dozens of old bottles, most of which are empty. The few that are not are full of a rich, red substance.
<br><br>
<<if $transformationParts.traits.sharpEyes isnot "default" and $TaylorWith isnot 1>>
	<span class="teal">With sharper eyes, you might find something of value down here.</span>
	<br><br>
<</if>>
<<if $rng lte 50 and $eventskip is 0>>
	<<forestmansionrandomevents>>
<<else>>
	<<if $TaylorWith is 1>>
		Taylor switches on <<his>> torch and looks around the room. "This must be the wine cellar. Our town used to pride itself on its high quality wine as a deluxe export. I can't believe some of this stuff still exists."
		<<if $museumAntiques.antiques.antiqueliquor is "notFound">>
			<<His>> torch glints off a bottle and <<he>> freezes. "Wait, is that a full bottle?! That is extremely rare!"
		<</if>>
		<br><br>
	<</if>>

	<<if $museumAntiques.antiques.antiqueliquor is "notFound" and ($transformationParts.traits.sharpEyes is "default" or $transformationParts.dragon.eyes isnot "disabled" or $TaylorWith is 1)>>
		<<link [[Take a bottle (0:02)|Forest Mansion Bottle Take]]>><<pass 2>><<museumAntiqueStatus "antiqueliquor" "found">><<set $antiquemoney += 5000>><</link>>
		<br>
		<<link [[Drink a bottle (0:02)|Forest Mansion Bottle Drink]]>><<pass 2>><<museumAntiqueStatus "antiqueliquor" "found">><<set $antiquemoney += 500>><<set $drunk += 480>><<set $hallucinogen += 80>><<npcincr Taylor love -1>><</link>> | <span class="red">+ + + + Alcohol</span> | <span class="red">+ + + Hallucinogen</span>
		<br>
	<</if>>

	<<link [[Go back to the kitchen (0:05)|Forest Mansion Kitchen]]>><<pass 5>><<set $eventskip to 0>><<set $rng to random(1,100)>><</link>>
<</if>>

:: Forest Mansion Bottle Take
You pull one of the still-full bottles from where it rested, giving it a good lookover. Between its rich colour, and its potential age, you are certain it would sell well. You pocket it for now, reminding yourself to seek out a collector later.
<br><br>
<<if $TaylorWith is 1>>
	"Hey what do you think you're doing? That's a priceless part of our town's history."
<</if>>
<br><br>

<<if $TaylorWith is 1>>
	<<link [[Tell saving for later|Forest Mansion Save For Later]]>><<npcincr Taylor love -1>><</link>>
	<br>
	<<link [[Tell giving to museum|Forest Mansion Giving to Museum]]>><<npcincr Taylor love 3>><</link>>
<<else>>
	<<link [[Next|Forest Mansion Cellar]]>><</link>>
<</if>>

:: Forest Mansion Save For Later
<<set $TaylorSaveForLater to 1>>
You tell Taylor that you're saving it to drink later against <<his>> wishes. <<He>> looks upset and shakes his head dropping the subject. <<llove>>
<br><br>

<<link [[Next|Forest Mansion Cellar]]>><</link>>

:: Forest Mansion Giving to Museum
You inform Taylor that you intend to give the wine to the museum for safe keeping. Taylor looks surprised and says "That's actually a good idea, nice going." <<gglove>>
<br><br>

<<link [[Next|Forest Mansion Cellar]]>><</link>>

:: Forest Mansion Bottle Drink
Popping the cork off, you take a big swig from the bottle. It's sweet, and causes a strange warmth to spread through your body. From just a single sip, you start to feel dizzy.
<br><br>
You consider stopping, but you can't pull your lips from the bottle. By the time you do, you've already drunk every last drop.
<br><br>
You think it's best you not do that again.
<br><br>

<<if $TaylorWith is 1>>
	"Hey what do you think you're doing? That's a priceless part of our town's history." <<llove>>
	<br><br>

	You shrug it off and finish the bottle and put the empty bottle back.
	<br><br>
<</if>>

<<link [[Next|Forest Mansion Cellar]]>><</link>>

:: Forest Mansion Dining Room
<<set $outside to 0>><<location "abandoned_mansion">><<set $forestmansionstage to 5>><<effects>>
You enter a large dining room. A long table stretches across most of it, still prepared for a feast that will never come.
<br><br>

<<if $rng lte 50 and $eventskip is 0>>
	<<forestmansionrandomevents>>
<<else>>

	<<if $TaylorWith is 1>>
		"This is certainly strange. Why would this table still be set if the owner moved out. The servants would have definitely needed to clean it up after the meal. It's almost as if everyone in the house just disappeared."
	<</if>>

	<<link [[Go back to the hallway (0:05)|Forest Mansion Left Hallway]]>><<pass 5>><<set $eventskip to 0>><<set $rng to random(1,100)>><</link>>
<</if>>

:: Forest Mansion Right Hallway
<<set $outside to 0>><<location "abandoned_mansion">><<set $forestmansionstage to 6>><<effects>>
You stand in the mansion's left hallway. The floorboards creak with every step you take.
<br><br>
Of the many rooms lining the hall, two in particular catch your eye. 
<br><br>

<<if $rng lte 50 and $eventskip is 0>>
	<<forestmansionrandomevents>>
<<else>>

	<<link [[Enter the servant quarters (0:05)|Forest Mansion Servant Quarters]]>><<pass 5>><<set $eventskip to 0>><<set $rng to random(1,100)>><</link>>
	<br>
	<<link [[Enter the master's study (0:05)|Forest Mansion Study]]>><<pass 5>><<set $eventskip to 0>><<set $rng to random(1,100)>><</link>>
	<br>
	<<link [[Towards the entrance (0:05)|Forest Mansion Entrance]]>><<pass 5>><<set $eventskip to 0>><<set $rng to random(1,100)>><</link>>
	<br>
<</if>>

:: Forest Mansion Servant Quarters
<<set $outside to 0>><<location "abandoned_mansion">><<set $forestmansionstage to 7>><<effects>>
You enter a cluttered room lined with beds in various states of disarray. Many are unmade, and a few have even collapsed. The wardrobe door hangs off its hinges, and any clothes that once filled it are long gone.
<br><br>
Cleaning supplies lie untouched in the corner of the room.
<br><br>

<<if $rng lte 50 and $eventskip is 0>>
	<<forestmansionrandomevents>>
<<else>>

	<<if $TaylorWith is 1>>
		"Wow the servants quarters seems to be a lot worse off than most of what we've seen. Servants must have been given a lot lower quality furniture. That or there was some kind of event that led to the room looking so... destroyed." 
		<br><br>
	<</if>>

	<<getouticon>><<link [[Go back to the hallway (0:05)|Forest Mansion Right Hallway]]>><<pass 5>><<set $eventskip to 0>><<set $rng to random(1,100)>><</link>>
<</if>>

:: Forest Mansion Study
<<set $outside to 0>><<location "abandoned_mansion">><<set $forestmansionstage to 8>><<effects>>
You walk into a large room lined with bookshelves. A desk rests in the middle, decorated with little props and stacks of old, faded papers. This is where the master of the manor would have worked. Most of the books are much, much older than the manor itself, falling apart from the slightest handling. A few, however, remain intact, and are still capable of being read.
<br><br>
While a bit outdated, they seem to be a great source of study.
<br><br>

<<if $rng lte 50 and $eventskip is 0>>
	<<forestmansionrandomevents>>
<<else>>

	<<if $TaylorWith is 1>>
		"It's a shame these books are so destroyed, they could have been something undocumented or important historical records." Taylor looks upset. "I'll take some anyway. Maybe I can find a way to restore them."
		<br><br>
	<</if>>

	<<scienceicon>><<link [[Study science (0:20)|Manor Study]]>><<scienceskill>><<pass 20>><<set $phase to 1>><</link>><<gscience>>
	<br>
	<<mathicon>><<link [[Study maths (0:20)|Manor Study]]>><<mathsskill>><<pass 20>><<set $phase to 2>><</link>><<gmaths>>
	<br>
	<<englishicon>><<link [[Study English (0:20)|Manor Study]]>><<englishskill>><<pass 20>><<set $phase to 3>><</link>><<genglish>>
	<br>
	<<historyicon>><<link [[Study history (0:20)|Manor Study]]>><<historyskill>><<pass 20>><<set $phase to 4>><</link>><<ghistory>>
	<br>
	<<getouticon>><<link [[Go back to the hallway (0:05)|Forest Mansion Right Hallway]]>><<pass 5>><<set $eventskip to 0>><<set $rng to random(1,100)>><</link>>
<</if>>

:: Forest Mansion Landing
<<set $outside to 0>><<location "abandoned_mansion">><<set $forestmansionstage to 9>><<effects>>
You climb your way to the upper landing, careful to avoid the steps rotted by time. At the top rests a hallway adorned wall to wall with large paintings, intimidation in each looming presence. At both ends of the hall lie doorways leading to other rooms.
<br><br>

<<if $rng lte 50 and $eventskip is 0>>
	<<forestmansionrandomevents>>
<<else>>

	<<link [[Go left to the guest suite (0:05)|Forest Mansion Guest Suite]]>><<pass 5>><<set $eventskip to 0>><<set $rng to random(1,100)>><</link>>
	<br>
	<<link [[Go right to the master suite (0:05)|Forest Mansion Master Suite]]>><<pass 5>><<set $eventskip to 0>><<set $rng to random(1,100)>><</link>>
	<br>
	<<link [[Go downstairs (0:05)|Forest Mansion Entrance]]>><<pass 5>><<set $eventskip to 0>><<set $rng to random(1,100)>><</link>>
<</if>>

:: Forest Mansion Guest Suite
<<set $outside to 0>><<location "abandoned_mansion">><<set $forestmansionstage to 10>><<effects>>
You find yourself in a nicely built and kept bedroom. The room looks almost unused, lying under a thin blanket of dust. The bed is made and there's still clothes in the wardrobe. Most are in remarkably good condition.
<br><br>

<<if $rng lte 50 and $eventskip is 0>>
	<<forestmansionrandomevents>>
<<else>>

	<<bedicon>><<link [[Sleep|Forest Mansion Bed]]>><</link>>
	<br>
	<<wardrobeicon>><<link [[Wardrobe|Forest Mansion Wardrobe]]>><</link>>
	<br>
	<<mirroricon>><<link [[Mirror|Forest Mansion Mirror]]>><</link>>
	<br>
	<<link [[Settings|Forest Mansion Settings]]>><<endevent>><</link>>
	<br>
	<<attitudesControlCheck>>
