<<settings>>

:: Mansion Jordan 1
The two of you walk through the forest, into the cemetery, and finally up to the door of the old, decrepit manor where you last felt your own flesh and blood.
<br><br>
"Do not fear. We are safe." Jordan looks at you. It brings some comfort. "Now, let's go get your body back." 
<<if $forestmansionpicked is 0>>
	<<He>> goes to open the door, but finds it locked. <<He>> frowns. "Ah. That's not good."
	<br><br>
	<<He>> turns to you, "do you know another way inside?"
	<br><br>
	<<link [[Pick lock (0:05)|Forest Mansion Pick Lock Jordan]]>><<pass 5>><</link>>
	<br>
	<<link [[Look around (0:20)|Forest Mansion Look Jordan]]>><<pass 30>><</link>>
<<else>>
	<<He>> grips the door handle and it opens with ease, the lock already picked open.
	<<link [[Next (0:05)|Mansion Jordan 2]]>><<pass 5>><</link>>
<</if>>

:: Forest Mansion Pick Lock Jordan
<<set $lock to 1000>>
<<effects>>
<<if $skulduggery gte $lock>>
	<<set $forestmansionpicked to 1>>
	<<skulduggeryskilluse>>
	With a grin, you approach the door, picking at the one-of-a-kind lock with absolute precision. At the sound of a heavy click, you rise up, opening the door and gesturing for Jordan to enter. 
	<br><br>
	"I don't think I should be promoting this behavior," <<he>> says. "But on this occasion, I think I can let it slide. Just make sure you aren't doing anything wrong, alright?"
	<br><br>
	The two of you head inside.
	<br><br>
	<<link [[Next|Mansion Jordan 2]]>><</link>>
<<else>>
	You try to pick at the lock, but find it to be unlike any you have ever seen before. After a bit of struggling, you give up.
	<br><br>
	"Perhaps we should look around for another way forward," Jordan suggests, offering a comforting hand on the shoulder. The two of you scour the outside for any entryways, eventually finding an open window. Jordan looks reluctant to enter, but eventually enters alongside you.
	<br><br>
	The two of you head inside.
	<br><br>
	<<link [[Next|Mansion Jordan 2]]>><</link>>
<</if>>

:: Forest Mansion Look Jordan
You suggest looking around further. The two of you scour the outside for any entryways, eventually finding an open window. Jordan looks hesitant to enter, but eventually enters alongside you.
<br><br>
The two of you head inside.
<br><br>
<<link [[Next|Mansion Jordan 2]]>><</link>>

:: Mansion Jordan 2
You guide <<him>> to the bedroom in which you slept only to find it empty.
<br><br>
"Looks like your body's been taken." <<He>> frowns. From what seems like out of nowhere, <<he>> pulls out a white powder. He spreads it in the air and it reveals a slimy trail along the ground, one which Jordan begins to follow.
<br><br>
<<link [[Next|Mansion Jordan 3]]>><</link>>

:: Mansion Jordan 3
You join <<him>>, tailing it through the house and into the kitchen. The slime stops at the edge of the trapdoor.
<br><br>
"Seems like our spirit is hiding in the cellar. Be careful." <<He>> casts you a cautionary glance before opening the trapdoor and climbing down.
<br><br>
<<link [[Next|Mansion Jordan 4]]>><</link>>

:: Mansion Jordan 4
You follow after Jordan, climbing down into the dark, damp cellar. Liquid drips from the ceiling as Jordan reaches into <<his>> robe and lights up a torch.
<br><br>
A mix of broken bottles and rich, red fluid are scattered across the floor, and large casks block your view. You hear something growl, deep and guttural, at the back of the room. It causes goosebumps to rise across your arms.
<br><br>
Jordan steps around a cask and shines <<his>> flame around. A rat skitters out of the light, but there's no sign of your body.
<br><br>
The growling soon stops. The two of you are left in silence until something lunges from the shadows. It aims for Jordan, causing <<him>> to pull out <<his>> whip and strike. The torch drops from <<his>> hand and spins towards your feet.
<br><br>
You hurriedly snatch it up and illuminate the scene. Within the dim torch light you find Jordan holding back against your thin, starved body. Your cheeks are sunken in, and your eyes nearly entirely black.
<br><br>
Jordan shouts something as <<he>> smashes a glass bottle on your body's forehead. Your body wails in pain, crumpling to the ground.
<br><br>
"Hurry! Hold it down!" Jordan yells as <<he>> removes the tome from <<his>> robe and opens to a bookmark.
<br><br>
<<link [[Next|Mansion Jordan 5]]>><</link>>

:: Mansion Jordan 5
You hold down your body as Jordan begins to read from the old tome. You don’t understand the language, but your body starts to twitch and scream in agony.
<br><br>
Black fluid pours from your body's pores and pools onto the ground as it continues to writhe and wail beneath you.
<br><br>
"Now! Before it can take hold once more!" Jordan yells. "Dive back inside! Force your way in!"
<br><br>
You waste no time following <<his>> orders. You shove yourself back into your own frame, phasing in and blacking out.  
<br><br>
<<link [[Next (6:00)|Mansion Jordan 6]]>><<clearExtraTransformations>><<pass 360>><</link>>

:: Mansion Jordan 6
You fling yourself up with a start, eyes flickering around the room wildly. You're in a plush, clean bed. Only a few meters away sits Jordan sleeping peacefully in a chair. Finally, you look down, and see your skin is once again normal. You feel relieved.
<br><br>
As you start to rise, Jordan wakes up. With a smile, <<he>> approaches. "Good morning, <<if $temple_rank is "monk" or $temple_rank is "priest">><<sister>><<else>>child<</if>>," <<he>> mumbles sleepily. "It seems like the exorcism took a lot out of us both. I barely made it back to the temple before passing out."
<br><br>
<<He>> helps you up. "I'm glad I could help with your spiritual problem. Next time, please try not to stay in such a cursed place."
<br><br>
<<He>> walks you back to the main room of the temple and bids you farewell. 
<br><br>
<<link [[Next|Temple]]>><<set $exorcism to 0>><<set $exorcised to 1>><</link>>